  "name": "URINE KETONE",
  "code": "URINE KETONE",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul><li>Negative: No ketones are detected in the urine. This is a normal result and indicates that the body is not producing ketones, or that ketones are being produced at a normal rate and are being used for energy.&nbsp;</li><li>Trace: A small amount of ketones is detected in the urine. This may indicate that the body is beginning to produce ketones, such as during fasting or prolonged exercise, or that the body is not able to use ketones efficiently. Additional monitoring may be necessary.&nbsp;</li><li>Small to Moderate: A moderate amount of ketones is detected in the urine. This may indicate that the body is producing a significant amount of ketones, such as during uncontrolled diabetes or in a state of ketosis due to a low-carbohydrate diet. Further evaluation by a healthcare provider is recommended.&nbsp;</li><li>Large: A large amount of ketones is detected in the urine. This is an abnormal result and may indicate a serious medical condition such as diabetic ketoacidosis, which requires immediate medical attention.<br></li></ul>",
